From: SP11 kernel worker <kernel-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH candidate] ASoC: qcom: bind SP11 calibration to the VI graph

The guard marks R0/T0 after SET_CFG, before a VI graph is prepared or
started. Closing an unstarted graph skips the stream-stop path, so its
calibration mask can survive and satisfy a later graph whose calibration
file is missing or invalid.

Invalidate calibration before VI setup and calibration, after setup or
start failures, and when a VI graph closes, including before start. Clear
it on every calibration error. A successful R0/T0 send is accepted only if
its generation has not been invalidated. Match the calibration's shared
AudioReach graph to the running VI graph before permitting unmute.

Serialize VI calibration sends. Multiple distinct running VI graphs are
ambiguous to the global guard and remain refused until all VI graphs stop;
closing a shared graph can likewise conservatively mute a remaining user.
When a reset turns an allowed state into a refused one, queue the existing
mute work. Preserve all existing protection and speaker policy checks.

---
